[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke-260527", :doc/title "ADR-2605262500 Operator Runbook Smoke — cycle 44 (2026-05-27)", :doc/status "active", :doc/doc_type "reference", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/body "\n# ADR-2605262500 Operator Runbook Smoke — cycle 44\n\nEmpirical evidence that the cycle 42 operator runbook actually works\nend-to-end. Each step of the runbook was executed from a fresh shell\n(no operator-side model install / no Mapillary token) to verify the\ndocumented commands behave as the runbook claims.\n\n**Smoke date**: 2026-05-27\n**Cycle**: 44 of /loop\n**Branch**: `feat/yakushi-wave-1c-r1-commissioning`\n**Environment**: macOS dev box; no rasterio, no operator-supplied ONNX models\n\n## Smoke matrix\n\n| # | Runbook step | Command | Expected | Observed | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Quick start preflight | `python3 70-tools/scripts/diagnose/e7m_preflight.py --filter ADR-2605262500 --skip-pds-network` | exit 1 (vision_pii_diagnose fails on no FACE_MODEL — operator action item printed) | exit 1; \"PREFLIGHT: FAIL (3/4 checks)\"; operator action items printed | ✓ matches doc |\n| 2 | vision_pii_diagnose check | `PYTHONPATH=... python3 -m e7m_dataset.vision_pii_diagnose check` | Required deps ✓, env all unset, classify skipped | exit as documented; deps OK; env unset; classify skipped | ✓ |\n| 3 | assemble_diagnose check | `python3 70-tools/e7m-sim/scripts/assemble_diagnose.py check` | yaml + recommended deps + scene schema + scene count | 11 scenes registered (8 ADR-2605262500 + 1 cartpole + 2 parallel-cycle additions: hikari + wadachi-hydro-micro) | ✓ |\n| 4 | assemble_diagnose inspect wadachi | `... inspect 70-tools/e7m-sim/scenes/wadachi-r1-shibuya-1km/scene.yaml` | wadachi-r1-shibuya-1km / 4 layers / max_tier A / charter scope | scene_name + ADR + 4 layers w/ dispatch handlers + CIDs + charter scan stub | ✓ |\n| 5 | assemble_diagnose dry-run wadachi | `... dry-run ...` | usda_bytes + sha256 prefix + \"no files written\" | usda_bytes=203664 sha256=`c76f6c7fb402…` \"(no files written)\" | ✓ |\n| 6 | Production assemble | `python3 70-tools/e7m-sim/scripts/assemble-usd-scene.py ... --out $tmp` | scene.usda + manifest.json written | both files written; usda_sha256 matches dry-run | ✓ |\n| 7 | G11 eval scalar PASS | `python3 70-tools/e7m-sim/scripts/eval_sim_metrics.py --psnr-db 28.5 --ssim 0.91 --chamfer-m 0.032 --iou 0.81` | GATE: PASS, exit 0 | exit 0; composite 0.7700; all per-metric pass | ✓ |\n| 8 | G11 eval --json | `... --json` | structured JSON with passed=true | JSON with values, norms, thresholds, per_metric_passed all true | ✓ |\n| 9 | Book-keeping verifier (ADR scope) | `python3 70-tools/scripts/lint/verify_deps_toml_paths.py --filter ADR-2605262500` | 40/40 entries resolve | exit 0; \"40/40 entries resolve; All paths resolve. Clean.\" | ✓ |\n| 10 | pds_diagnose parse smoke | `PYTHONPATH=... python3 -m e7m_dataset.pds_diagnose parse \"at://...\"` | repo + collection + rkey printed | repo=did:web:dataset-pinner.etzhayyim.com / collection=com.etzhayyim.substrate.datasetPin / rkey=3kpqab | ✓ |\n\n**10 / 10 documented commands work as the runbook describes.**\n\n## USDA SHA observation\n\nDry-run (`assemble_diagnose dry-run`) and real assemble\n(`assemble-usd-scene.py`) produced **identical** usda_sha256 prefix\n`c76f6c7fb402…`. This confirms G6 determinism invariant — dry-run is a\nfaithful preview of the production output bytes.\n\n## Subtle behaviors confirmed\n\n1. **Preflight FAIL on no FACE_MODEL is operator-friendly**, not a runbook\n   bug. The printed \"operator action items\" guide the operator to the\n   per-tool diagnostics, which then point at the env-var fix.\n\n2. **assemble_diagnose runs standalone** (no e7m-dataset on PYTHONPATH)\n   and correctly falls back to the `stub-no-e7m-dataset` charter scope.\n   Operators who want the full Charter scan integration should set\n   `PYTHONPATH=70-tools/e7m-dataset/src` when running the diagnostics —\n   but production assemble does NOT depend on this (it uses the same\n   defensive fallback).\n\n3. **G11 eval scalar mode** is a smooth on-ramp for operators who\n   already have Isaac Sim metrics from an external test run — no need\n   to wire up image/point-cloud files yet.\n\n## What this smoke does NOT cover\n\nOperations requiring operator-side env that this smoke can't validate:\n\n- `e7m-dataset pull mapillary --token $MAPILLARY_TOKEN` (needs real Mapillary token)\n- Real ONNX face-detector smoke (`vision_pii_diagnose smoke`) needs an actual model file\n- `pds_diagnose resolve` against live `pds.etzhayyim.com` (needs network + real datasetPin record)\n- W2.4 rasterio path (needs `pip install rasterio`)\n\nThese are all \"operator-side env prep\" that the runbook directs the\noperator to set up. The runbook smoke confirms the **paths that\nshould work without operator setup actually do work**.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nRunbook is **production-ready as written**. No content changes needed\nfrom this smoke. One small operator-side hint that could be added (but\nisn't blocking): mention `PYTHONPATH=70-tools/e7m-dataset/src` when\nrunning e7m-sim diagnostics if the operator wants the full Charter\nscan integration (vs the defensive stub fallback).\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-operator-runbook-260527.edn` (runbook subject of this smoke)\n- `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-implementation-retrospective-260527.edn` (cycle 40 history)\n- ADR-2605262500 (canonical)\n", :doc/path "90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke-260527.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/topic "adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-27", :doc/date "2026-05-27", :doc/authoritative false, :doc/related ["doc-adr-2605262500-operator-runbook-260527" "doc-adr-2605262500-implementation-retrospective-260527"], :doc/authoritative_for ["empirical evidence that the cycle 42 operator runbook works end-to-end"]}]
